WEBVTT

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.200
<i>Joe...</i>

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.900
<i>Now that I've seen this fight, I can see that Rikiishi is still a step ahead of you.</i>

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:52.800
<i>Rikiishi's uppercuts are his trump card against your No Guard strategy.</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.880
<i>Now listen, Joe.</i>

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.930
<i>No matter how invincible your Cross Counter is,</i>

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:02.030
<i>you won't gain anything from it unless your opponent throws a straight.</i>

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:08.730
<i>And Rikiishi will avoid that by throwing uppercuts, which only go up!</i>

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.310
<i>That's why...</i>

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.350
<i>That's why,</i>

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.230
<i>as long as Rikiishi never throws a straight,</i>

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.350
<i>your No Guard strategy may as well have already lost!</i>

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.610
<i>May as well have already lost...</i>

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:23.510
Hey, old man.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.290
I wouldn't throw my No Guard strategy out the window just yet.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.890
What? Say that again.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.770
Sure, I'll say it as many times as you want.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.250
I'm gonna improve my No Guard strategy!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.860
In other words, my No Guard is the only thing I can rely on, just like it's always been!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.730
You idiot! Have you gone mad from seeing how Rikiishi rendered the Cross Counter useless?

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:07.120
Don't you get that your No Guard won't do a thing against his uppercut strategy?

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.890
I know, but...

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.170
I see. Guess a verbal explanation ain't enough for you, old man.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:16.920
What?

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:18.690
Never mind, never mind.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.920
This is just a generational gap.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.690
It was my mistake to try and explain something to a decrepit old man.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:28.720
Decrepit!?

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.040
I've gotta show this to you in action.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.200
All right, old man! Put on the gloves and get in the ring!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.290
Looks like you've come up with another stupid idea.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.090
All right, explain!

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.050
Okay.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.140
Listen up, old man.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.510
This is what we got out of the match.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:11.590
Rikiishi's gonna use an uppercut-heavy strategy to keep me from throwing the Cross Counter.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:19.270
But...

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:26.990
But what's gonna happen if I get all serious and tighten my guard against it?

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:33.000
Now, hit me with the hardest uppercut you got, like the one from your glory days, old man!

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.000
The hardest?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.000
Yeah.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.970
All right. I may be old, but you should know how strong my punches are!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.550
I know, just get on with it! Now!

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.010
Right, here I come!

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.960
H-Hey, Joe! You all right?

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.010
I warned you, didn't I?

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:26.510
Heh, that's nothing.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.890
I intentionally weakened my guard just to experiment, you decrepit fart.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.010
What?

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.430
But that's good enough.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.270
If Rikiishi's uppercut hits me head-on,

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.020
and I have a half-baked guard, it'll be the exact same!

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.520
I get it.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.390
You're right. Guards are good at protecting against frontal attacks,

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.490
but you could still be blown away by an uppercut coming from below.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:53.490
Yeah. And that's where my style comes in.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.000
With both arms hanging loose.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:58.890
All right, decrepit old man!

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.450
I know this may be tough for you,

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.870
but this time, why don't you try landing about a dozen uppercuts on me?

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.870
I've had just about enough of your lip!

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:06.840
Here I go!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:08.260
Yeah!

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.220
Hey, where do you think you're going, old man?

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.810
I was just a bit off, idiot!

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.090
Oh, really?

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.780
It looked to me like your decrepit legs couldn't keep up!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:28.960
Dammit, I'm pulling out all the stops now!

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.470
What's the matter, old man?

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.380
Don't tell me you were missing on purpose!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.110
No.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.840
Well, looks like you've finally caught on.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.530
But just like Leo showed us that night,

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.200
the best tactic against a huge uppercut

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:59.470
is to sway back, moving your upper body to make it miss.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.530
And the No Guard stance, with both arms swinging loose, is the best position for that.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.830
If I put up a half-baked guard, I'd start to rely on it,

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:09.830
and I wouldn't be able to move as flexibly.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.470
Y-You have a point.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:16.700
I guess you're just a hair away from being a genius when it comes to boxing.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.290
So first I'm an idiot, and now I'm a genius?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.970
Man, it's real tiring going back and forth like that!

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.290
But it's too soon to celebrate!

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:34.800
Rikiishi's ability is also genius-level!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.310
And his uppercuts are far from average!

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:45.230
Hey, Nishi!

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:47.070
Nishi!

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:48.910
Coming.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.270
Whaddya want?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.750
Don't give me that!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.510
Put on your gloves and get in the ring, now!

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:57.580
I-In the ring?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.580
I said now!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.090
What's the matter, old man?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.670
You're so tired, you're switching out with Nishi?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.290
No. We're gonna do some sparring.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.090
Two-on-one.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:19.370
T-Two-on-one?

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.600
Yes. Two-on-one.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:26.830
Rikiishi's uppercuts are on a whole other level from mine, in strength, speed, and quantity.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:32.570
To overcome that, Nishi and I will come at you with all four of our arms.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.620
I get it. That's a pretty great idea-for you.

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.390
I don't think I need to mention this, but this is Sway Back training.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:51.090
You can't punch back at us, Joe.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.210
All right, already!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.230
Listen, Nishi.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:59.090
You can attack with me, from the front, or to the side!

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:01.470
Just hit Joe with uppercuts!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.470
B-But if we attack Joe together, and he can't counterattack...

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.280
Stop complaining and just do it!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.210
Yeah! No need to hold back, Nishi!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.390
But, Joe...

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:14.210
Enough complaining, Nishi.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.930
Get over here and line up next to me!

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:16.870
Right.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.000
Now, whenever you're ready.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:27.540
Let's go, Nishi!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.090
R-Right!

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:37.510
Well, it really makes a difference taking on you both at once! It's definitely a lot more intense!

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.840
Quit your babbling!

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:40.600
Get him, Nishi!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.030
Joe!

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:59.530
Nishi, quit worrying and pour some water on him!

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:01.490
Joe...

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:02.990
Water?

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.370
Yeah!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.830
I'm going outside for a breather.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:08.460
Old man...

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:14.910
Joe...

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:19.410
You have to do everything you can to endure this bloody training!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:22.550
You have no other hope of victory.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:28.150
After all, Rikiishi is enduring an impossible drop in weight just to fight you!

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.710
You have to stick with it, Joe!

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.330
What a pathetic bastard!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.710
Pour another bucket on him!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.720
Gimme the bucket, Nishi.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.720
O-Okay.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.230
What's the matter? Done already?

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.770
Don't make me laugh.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.450
I'm not down for the count, but...

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.930
The arms-hanging Sway Back...

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.130
This training to dodge Rikiishi's uppercut...

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.190
Will doing this...

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.960
Will doing this

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.210
let me win?

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:40.970
Rikiishi's going through an incredible drop in weight to prepare for our fight.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.310
Can I beat him?

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.530
Hey look, we've got some reporters here!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.090
Good day, everyone!

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.410
Is Yabuki-kun practicing now?

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:11.950
Sure, he is. At least, it looks like he is. He's pretty active.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.070
By the way, how 'bout it?

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:17.540
How 'bout a drink to celebrate Joe knocking out Rikiishi ahead o' time?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.090
N-No, we're on the job!

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.090
Come on, it'll be fine!

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:26.070
Man, oh man. These guys think he's already won the Rikiishi match.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:30.590
After all, people around here think Joe's some kind of all-powerful god.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.690
Hey, kid.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.090
Sorry to bother you, but would you let me by?

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:44.700
Thanks a lot.

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.700
Excuse me.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.580
Who's there?

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:57.140
W-We're from Toto Sports...

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.580
Who told you you could come in?

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.590
W-Well, uh...

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.090
Get out!

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:04.590
But...

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.300
Out!

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:12.770
And don't come back!

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.010
That scared me.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.650
It's like he's gone insane.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.270
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.280
We got kicked out because of you!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.610
W-We're sorry. Just don't get so mad at us.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.450
But does Tange Gym always practice that intensely?

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:31.410
Say what?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.370
Tange Gym's famous for its bloody training! Got it?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.790
Hey!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.790
Come here for a sec!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.040
O-Okay.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.530
I see.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:44.870
This is just perfect.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.970
They're peeping!

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.530
They're peeping!

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.810
Old man!

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:55.990
Please! We're at work here!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.730
Just let us go this once, okay?

00:13:58.130 --> 00:13:59.730
Let you go?

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.690
For free?

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.400
With no charge?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.460
U-Uh, this isn't much, but maybe you can go buy a treat or something...

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:21.530
Well, it's not much, but I'll take it.

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:24.590
I can't say I don't understand you reporters' position.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.290
Good, good.

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:30.510
But just you try and write an article that does Joe wrong!

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.010
You'll pay for it!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.020
We'll kick you down, then smash and smush and squish-

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.730
And squash and smash and smush you!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:40.230
Got that, you hacks?

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:41.810
There, I said it!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.150
All right, now let's go to the oden stand at the corner!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:48.440
Let's go get some spaghetti at that restaurant on the thoroughfare!

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.950
Man, oh man...

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.950
<i>What a handful.</i>

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.950
Hey, old man!

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.650
They're peeping!

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.960
F-Fine. Go and buy yourselves a drink.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.870
It worked! Let's get some sake at the sake house!

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:08.310
Idiot, let's go to a beer hall!

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.690
You seem to be pretty beat.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.410
Let's leave it at that for today.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.700
D-Don't stop now!

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.200
Keep it going!

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.250
Please keep going, old man!

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.790
I don't wanna do this anymore!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:46.870
I can't keep this up! I can't keep on hitting you when you're already a bloody pulp!

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:49.710
Idiot! I said I'm fine, so I'm fine!

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:50.800
Pull yourself together, Nishi!

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.800
Give me a break...

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.050
I'm just about to get it!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.760
Now, hit me with your best shot!

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.290
What's he about to get?

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:01.470
What the hell are those three gonna do?

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.270
Come on! Bring it!

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:05.570
Nishi.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:07.150
Y-Yes.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.070
Let's go.

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:17.030
What's the matter, Nishi? Get in the fight!

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.540
All right, let's go!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.500
Yeah, that's it!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.930
That's good! Keep punching and punching and punching, Nishi!

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.130
Good, good!{added by editor}

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:36.720
What's the matter? Can't you punch any harder?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.220
Or are you worn out already?

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.750
Well, I don't blame you.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.890
Missing an uppercut means double the swing.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.190
So it uses up double the energy!

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.690
I didn't think you still had enough juice in you to theorize!

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:51.280
Go, Nishi!

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.280
Keep on punching!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.270
Almost there.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.980
I've almost got it. I'm nearly there!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.210
I can't do this!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.850
If this keeps up, you'll be crippled before the match!

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:32.900
Dumbass!

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.270
If...

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.650
If you don't

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:41.660
want to see me beaten up by Rikiishi and coughing blood on the day of the match...

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.390
If you don't...

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.670
Then you gotta punch me now!

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.990
Now, get up and punch!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.210
But...

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.210
C'mon! Punch!

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.930
Nishi, this is what Joe wants.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:17:59.650
Come on!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:17.350
They're attacking him with uppercut after uppercut, then they suddenly throw a straight...

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:21.490
They must've come up with that strategy by watching Rikiishi.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:27.320
I see it!

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.930
That's enough! I've had enough of covering this!

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.410
That hurt to watch!

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.390
Was that even boxing practice?

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.050
I don't know.

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:55.330
Rikiishi's been losing so much weight, he's going into the match looking like a mummy.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.240
Will they last until they meet in the ring?

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.840
Even if they do...

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:04.240
Maybe they'll both end up losing.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.810
Joe, I think you'd better stop.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:32.770
What?

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:37.110
Once a man's eyes get too used to seeing uppercuts,

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:42.540
he'll fall into the trap of not being able to adjust to different punches.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.710
I'm coughing up blood and refusing to quit

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.750
so that I won't fall into his trap.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.390
Now, if you have time to give me that bullshit again,

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.760
let's do this over! Just the same as before!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.720
Nishi!

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.490
Old man!

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:25.240
Well, let's go.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.240
You'll be sorry if you pull your punches!

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.930
I can see it!

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.370
But I won't hold back either.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.750
I'll throw a hard punch when I think I can win!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.150
Sounds good. Right, Nishi?

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:39.770
Yeah!

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:16.420
Now!

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:21.070
I see it! Now!

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:23.870
Old man!

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.630
Old man! Stay with us!

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:39.000
Old man! Hang in there!

00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:42.050
You awake, old man?

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:47.750
I did it, old man.

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:51.090
Once you went from throwing uppercuts to a straight,

00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:53.470
I turned that straight into a Cross Counter!

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:56.000
You did it! You did it, Joe!

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:04.480
Well, it looks like you don't have to be worried about Rikiishi's uppercuts anymore.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:05.310
Yeah.

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:07.090
But don't lose focus just yet.

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:10.490
Your opponent may have countless other trump cards up his sleeve.

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:13.470
Just trust me.

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:16.540
I'll be two or three times as confident when I'm in the ring!

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:41.060
Joe's training

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:43.100
continues night and day.

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:47.400
Meanwhile, as Rikiishi endures his fierce weight loss,

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:49.690
he finally loses control, unable to bear his thirst.

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:54.910
Rikiishi rampages like a madman in search of water in his dark cellar.

00:23:56.050 --> 00:24:01.590
Now, as Rikiishi faces his ultimate crisis before his showdown with Joe,

00:24:01.590 --> 00:24:03.080
which way is tomorrow!?

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.100
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.100
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:21.180 --> 00:24:23.940
Oira boxer

00:24:21.180 --> 00:24:23.940
I am a boxer.

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:31.700
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:31.700
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:33.410 --> 00:24:37.370
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:33.410 --> 00:24:37.370
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:37.370 --> 00:24:39.410
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:37.370 --> 00:24:39.410
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:45.630
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:45.630
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:48.630
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:48.630
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

